<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_Buttons @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_Buttons @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</h1>


<p>
    Everything you need to work with the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-button</span> CSS class: the BEM classes it provides, the strongly-typed <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Button</span> C# object
    used to apply them, supporting enums, and the CSS variables used for styling.
</p>

<h2 class="page-heading">Overview</h2>

<p>
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-button</span> is a theme-reactive button element that shares its underlying styling - border radius, focus indicator, active/hover states - with every button used inside Blazor Ramp components.
</p>
<p>
    Colours are theme-reactive: they're built from the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-cls-*</span> variables described below, which in turn derive from the same
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-*</span> primitives used across every Blazor Ramp component. Changing your theme updates <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-button</span> automatically
    - no separate configuration needed.
</p>
<p>
    Unlike <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">@CodeSpan.Base</span> and <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-kbd</span>, solid colour scheme text colours for the base primary/secondary/accent/neutral/danger/warning/success/info
    schemes are computed automatically using the CSS <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">contrast-color()</span> function, since the underlying hue is user-themeable and cannot be predicted in advance.
    The lighter and darker scheme variants use fixed, curated text colours instead, since their contrast direction is always known.
</p>


<section>
    <h2 id="c#-classes" class="page-heading">C# API</h2>
    <p>
        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Button</span> provides the BEM CSS classes for the br-button block: a theme-reactive
        button element that shares its underlying styling with every Blazor Ramp component.
    </p>
    <section class="code-table">
        <h3 id="button-class" class="code-table__heading">Button class</h3>
        <table aria-labelledby="button-class">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Return</th>
                    <th scope="col">Const/Static Method</th>
                    <th scope="col">Description</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Button.Base</td>
                    <td>The base class, <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-button</span>. Always required.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Button.FullWidth</td>
                    <td>Makes the button take the full width of its container.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Button.Size(ButtonSize buttonSize)</td>
                    <td>Gets the class that sets the button's size.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme solidScheme)</td>
                    <td>Gets the class that sets the button's solid colour scheme: its background, border, and a contrasting text colour.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td>Button.FixedRadius(UnitRadius unitRadius)</td>
                    <td>
                        Gets the modifier class that sets the button's border radius to a
                        fixed unit value, bypassing the themeable default button group radius.
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>
</section>

