<section>
     <h2 class="page-heading">Usage</h2>
    <p>
        The following shows examples of the styles applied to buttons.
        <b>Note: </b>All of the CSS classes have variables for both light and dark schemes and the dark theme variables. Click the Theme button at the top of the page.
    </p>
    <p>
        The following shows an example styling the button to be a regular size without any scheme so the default button styles are applied.
    </p>
    <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CssClassesSnippets.Button_Regular_Default_Example" AriaLabel="Button styling code example" />
    <p>
       <button class="@Button.Base @Button.Size(ButtonSize.Regular)">Settings</button>
    </p>

    <h3>Default component styling</h3>
    <p>The component buttons are clear so just show the background colour.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap; gap:var(--br-unit-space-5);margin-block:var(--br-unit-space-5)">
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Size(ButtonSize.Small)">Default Small</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base">Default Regular</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Size(ButtonSize.Large)">Default Large</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Size(ButtonSize.ExtraLarge)">Default Extra Large</button>
    </div>
    
    <h3>Fixed central unit colour value from each of the colour palettes</h3>
    <p>
        Excluding the inverted scheme, the colour of the text for these are set via the CSS <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">contrast-color</span> function.
    </p>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap; gap:var(--br-unit-space-5);margin-block:var(--br-unit-space-5)">
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.Primary)">Solid Primary</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.Neutral)">Solid Neutral</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.Secondary)">Solid Secondary</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.Accent)">Solid Accent</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.Danger)">Solid Danger</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.Warning)">Solid Warning</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.Success)">Solid Success</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.Info)">Solid Info</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.Inverted)">Solid Inverted</button>
    </div>
    
    <h3>Uses the lighter shade with a darker text of the same colour from each colour palette</h3>

    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap; gap:var(--br-unit-space-5);margin-block:var(--br-unit-space-5)">
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.PrimaryLighter)">Solid Primary Lighter</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.NeutralLighter)">Solid Neutral Lighter</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.SecondaryLighter)">Solid Secondary Lighter</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.AccentLighter)">Solid Accent Lighter</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.DangerLighter)">Solid Danger Lighter</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.WarningLighter)">Solid Warning Lighter</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.SuccessLighter)">Solid Success Lighter</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.InfoLighter)">Solid Info Lighter</button>

    </div>
    
    <h3>Uses a darker shade with a lighter text of the same colour from each colour palette</h3>

    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap; gap:var(--br-unit-space-5);margin-block:var(--br-unit-space-5)">
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.PrimaryDarker)">Solid Primary Darker</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.NeutralDarker)">Solid Neutral Darker</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.SecondaryDarker)">Solid Secondary Darker</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.AccentDarker)">Solid Accent Darker</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.DangerDarker)">Solid Danger Darker</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.WarningDarker)">Solid Warning Darker</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.SuccessDarker)">Solid Success Darker</button>
        <button type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.InfoDarker)">Solid Info Darker</button>
    </div>

    <h3>Fixed border radius that does not respond to the button border group</h3>

     <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap; gap:var(--br-unit-space-5);margin-block:var(--br-unit-space-5)">
        <button class="@Button.Base @Button.FixedRadius(UnitRadius.Two)" >Default Regular With a Fixed Radius of 2</button>
        <button class="@Button.Base @Button.Scheme(ButtonSolidScheme.Neutral) @Button.FixedRadius(UnitRadius.Four)">Solid Neutral Large With a Fixed Radius of 4</button>
     </div>

</section>
